Gaussian EM/BLUP code, particularly sig(), bay() and logV(), is adapted from
MEGB 0.2, Gradient Boosting for Longitudinal Data (GPL-2), authored by
Oyebayo Ridwan Olaniran and Saidat Fehintola Olaniran.
Source: https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=MEGB
DOI: 10.32614/CRAN.package.MEGB

The release review compared these functions with MEGB 0.2. MEXGB changes include
extreme gradient boosting, cross-fitting, extended outcome families and revised
validation, numerical handling and documentation. Saidat Fehintola Olaniran is
credited as a contributor of the adapted code; this does not imply endorsement
or responsibility for the new implementation. Methodological references appear
in the manual and CITATION. Maintainers remain responsible for verifying any
additional source provenance and obtaining agreement from credited authors.
